    "text": "5. Full-Duplex Communication: > TCP offers full-duplex service, in which data can flow in both directions at the same time. 6. Connection-Oriented Service: > When a process at site A wants to send/receive data from another process at siteB. =| SO_ 1. The two TCPs establish a connection between them. 2. Data are exchanged in both directions. | bo -- —SS0 , 3. The connection is terminated. | > This ts a virtual connection, not a physical connection. > TCP accepts the responsibility of delivering the bytes in order to the other site. 7. Reliable Service: > It uses an acknowledgment mechanism to check the safe arrival of data.",
